A||||15||stsmithgt||I FAILED my smog test.:(||||8||
Z||000000||stsmithgt||10-19-2000||01:54 PM||||Oops This is a little long winded.(venting you know)<P>They told me my timing was off and that might help it pass. What the FU????? I wanted to know why they didn't adjust the timing right there and try it again, but they decided to charge me another 30 something dollars before touching it again.  They said it still might not pass.  Talk about covering there a$$ for failure.  These guys told me not to wait anymore.  They have no idea how long I've been waiting to drive my car and now they put me OFF!(steam rises from my head) I bet they'll put extra effort into the AC Cobra with the Ferrari engine that came in after mine to get smogged.  That thing sounded like it was dropping a load too. Yuk.  I'm sure I'm over reacting, but I'm tired of getting rides from other folks to get around and I'm not renting another car.  I forgot a pair of glasses in the last one. There went 175 bucks <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif">  Ok I'm done venting. <BR>So ends another chapter.||||reg||8
Z||000001||ThatRickGuy||10-19-2000||02:23 PM||||I feel your pain man. I'm from Wisconsin so I don't have to worry about smog laws. but when I first got to Virginia, I had to get my '76 ventura smoged, that was about a pain! When I bought the Fiero tho I took leave and went home to WI and registered in there so I don't have to worry about it now  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> It was kinda amusing when the gate guard asked me if I was aware my inspetion sticker was 2 years out of date  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> hehehehe||||reg||1
Z||000002||stsmithgt||10-19-2000||02:49 PM||||Yeah I used to register my vehicles at the neighborhood country club.  It was private so they had their own smog laws, which was none.  I miss those days. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> The law caught up with them and they have to smog like everyone else.  Man this makes me want to get a pre-1972 vehicle just so I feel like I'm getting back at those law makers with a set of headers, highrise and a nasty cam to turn the heads of the police. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  Of course that would be my second vehicle and the emissions would probably pass smog if I had it set up right(not visually).  Maybe a 4x4 with super swampers so I have something to park my car under. he he.||||reg||10
Z||000003||286SE'S||10-19-2000||03:05 PM||||If you cat has 75,000 miles on it or is original to the car, replace it. A new cat will usually kill all the tested pollutants to zero. My before and after cat tests results were night and day. This is assuming that you have gotten that timing correct. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000004||1FST2M6||10-19-2000||03:11 PM||||you fail NOx?<BR><P>------------------<BR>Shhh.. Top Secret! <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/1fstcheeto_2.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||stsmithgt||10-19-2000||03:55 PM||||They weren't specific about what failed except they said my timing was off.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/confused.gif">  From what I saw the way the mechanic crawled all over the car looking for a way to get the timing, I think he might of failed.  <BR>My CAT is about 15,000 miles old along with the muffler most of the other smog stuff.  No exhaust leaks.  Fixed last year with front manifold kit.  New plugs, New plug wires, had the pick up coil replaced, Cap and rotor on the distributor aren't a year old.  I don't burn oil. Smells good to me.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  My idle is a hair shakey(*no thanks to the dealership), but my Idle controll and sensor are fairly new.(replaced last summer).  The egr sensor, pipe are all under a year old.  I mean I've been pouring the $$$$.$$ into this thing constantly to keep it ship shape.  So this failure is giving me a major tension headache.  My fuse is getting short so these smog guys best give me some good news when I call.<BR>*The dealership was supposed to get rid of the shakey idle and all they did was set my last (NEW)set of MSD plug wires on fire by leaving them on the exhaust manifold.  I didn't check the monkeys work and ended up paying for it.<P>I want to go use that new kevlar clutch from the Fiero Shop without getting pulled over for something as trivial as registration stickers. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/BURNOUT.gif"> <p>[This message has been edited by stsmithgt (edited 10-19-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000006||1FST2M6||10-20-2000||08:03 AM||||ok with your "timing off" odds are your NOx is STOOPID high.. thus meaning your timing is fine and your EGR solenoid has failed. The emissions  (no so bright boy told me to change the timing in my car) I knew better after HOURS of dyno tuning.. I didn't have timing problems.. i put the car BAVK on the dyno and droped it un 4th under load at part throttle and looked at the EGR.. guess what yep.. it wasn't opening. you'll need a 18"-24" piece of 5/16 vacuum tubing run it from the top of the EGR to the TOP vacuum line on the trunk wall this will bypass the solenoid won't throw a code 32 and will help you fuel economy. AND make you pass emissions! good luck||||reg||1
Z||000007||stsmithgt||10-20-2000||09:30 AM||||Thanks for the tip.  Once I got my paper work from them, it said my timing was too far advanced.  I'm glad it wasn't more difficult to fix because the way he was looking at the stickers on my deck lid for information sorta scared me.<BR>     Well they keeping my car all day and $110.00+ later, I get my car back and it passed the test.  They said they had to retard the timing 10 degrees. What a stroke of genius.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"> I thought they were going to do that while I waited since I waited 45 minutes to get my car back in the first place.  I guess they liked my car so much they wanted it to sit in their parking lot all day.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> One guy couldn't get over my steering wheel.  He was playing "show and tell" with it around the lot while I paid my bill.  He didn't get to keep my steering wheel either TGOwens.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">he he <P><p>[This message has been edited by stsmithgt (edited 10-20-2000).]||||reg||1
