Z||000009||EdsB52||10-21-2000||09:04 PM||||I wish I had read that post before you dropped more money. I have rebuilt 2 each 2.5's but have the same problem regardless of age or condition of the engine. The timing is suppossed to be 8 degrees before, I set it right at TDC. It runs like sh!t, but my theory is that the smog testing unit measures percentages of the specific polutants, not gross amount. So possibly the HC's and whatever else support combustion better when more amounts exist (W.A.G.). I got the idea years ago when my girlfriends four year old Toyota, which had only 50,000 miles on it with a complete tune-up by me, failed misserably at the smog station. She ended up taking it to Tune-up Masters where they retarded the timing about 10 degrees. My girlfriend said it passed, but ran like sh!t, so I investigated and found the preceeding data.<P>Arizona allows owners of vehicles that are four years old or newer to waive smog inspections. My theory for this is that the state knows the test is bullsh!t and has been embarassed by new cars failing.||||reg||1
